# Building an object runs the initializer along its class's order: `Audit` has none of its own, so `Audit(path)` runs
# `Log.__init__`, which stamps the file it is handed. It runs none of the methods, `add` and `last` among them. The value
# it builds is an Audit, and the route prints the path the audit holds.

route auditlog.run
step run/Audit()
step run/Audit()/stamp

line entry > run call
line run/Audit()/stamp > Disk(run.path) own
line run/Audit() > Audit·audit@run/Audit() value
known #101 line Audit·audit@run/Audit() > run value       # run prints a field of the audit it built
line run > Screen own

home Audit·audit@run/Audit() run

side entry left
side Disk(run.path) right
side Screen right
